1
00:00:00,272 --> 00:00:01,168
Oh, no!

2
00:00:01,168 --> 00:00:02,368
Looks like I win again!

3
00:00:02,368 --> 00:00:05,776
Come on, Leafy. We have to play again. I have to win this time!

4
00:00:05,776 --> 00:00:09,248
Uh, I-I don't know, Firey. I hadn't planned on
playing Tic-Tac-Toe seventy-three times today.

5
00:00:09,248 --> 00:00:10,832
Come on, Leafy, please!

6
00:00:10,832 --> 00:00:12,512
Uh, actually, y-yeah, let's do it!

7
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:14,288
- ROCKY: Bleh!
- Oh, my gosh! Rocky just threw up!

8
00:00:14,288 --> 00:00:15,984
He might be sick! We have to go help him! NOW!

9
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:18,064
FIREY:
Hey, wait! Leafy! Come back!

10
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:18,979
- AAAAAAAAAAA!!!!

11
00:00:18,979 --> 00:00:21,920
- Leafy! Leafy! Oh, no, what happened?
- AAAAAAAAAAA!!!!

12
00:00:22,112 --> 00:00:23,888
EEEAAAHHH!!

13
00:00:25,408 --> 00:00:27,062
- Oh, my gosh! Oh, my gosh! What's happening!?

14
00:00:27,062 --> 00:00:28,624
- AAAHHH!
- Oh, my gosh! Oh, my gosh! What's happening!?

15
00:00:29,152 --> 00:00:29,760
ROCKY:
Bleh!

16
00:00:30,896 --> 00:00:32,704
Hey! I'm weightless!

17
00:00:32,704 --> 00:00:33,392
Wow!

18
00:00:33,392 --> 00:00:35,808
Hey, Radio? Why are we in space?

19
00:00:35,808 --> 00:00:37,584
Because of budget cuts.

20
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:44,480
♪ [INTRO PLAYS] ♪

21
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:46,480
Subtitles: Daniel Adam Valle

22
00:00:47,248 --> 00:00:50,624
Hey, Ice Cube, look! It's the Big Dipper!

23
00:00:50,896 --> 00:00:52,432
This star is for you!

24
00:00:52,432 --> 00:00:52,976
Thanks!

25
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:55,248
Huh? Oh, no, what happened to the Big Dipper?!

26
00:00:55,344 --> 00:00:57,120
And why are Bubble and Ice Cube playing catch?!

27
00:00:57,120 --> 00:01:00,848
Be quiet. Even though we are in
space, everything is still the same.

28
00:01:01,152 --> 00:01:03,456
So we will still have Cake at Stake.

29
00:01:04,048 --> 00:01:05,392
♪ The points are gone ♪

30
00:01:05,392 --> 00:01:08,512
♪ We are free of them now, but we look on ♪

31
00:01:09,630 --> 00:01:11,776
♪ To the moment that we see: ♪

32
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:14,240
♪ The next slice of cake ♪

33
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,384
♪ A step closer to the prize ♪

34
00:01:16,384 --> 00:01:18,496
♪ Brought on by Cake at Stake ♪

35
00:01:19,968 --> 00:01:23,664
Well, I learned that a normal cake
would explode in the vacuum of space.

36
00:01:23,664 --> 00:01:26,000
So instead, I got an ice cream cake.

37
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:26,608
Yum!

38
00:01:26,608 --> 00:01:28,000
Wait, how would that make any difference?

39
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:28,624
Hush!

40
00:01:28,624 --> 00:01:30,620
If you get cake, you are safe.

41
00:01:30,784 --> 00:01:32,704
Otherwise, you are eliminated.

42
00:01:32,704 --> 00:01:37,024
Bubble, Rocky, Firey, and Leafy
had immunity, so they get cake.

43
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:40,720
I know you love ice cream cake,
Bubble, so I'm giving you my cake!

44
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:41,504
Thanks!

45
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:44,784
Now it's down to David, Spongy, and Ice Cube.

46
00:01:45,264 --> 00:01:48,176
545 people voted this time.

47
00:01:48,608 --> 00:01:52,432
Seventy-two of them voted for Ice Cube, she is safe.

48
00:01:53,184 --> 00:01:56,112
So it's either Spongy or David to leave the game.

49
00:01:56,384 --> 00:01:59,312
Both entered the game late. Let's show the votes.

50
00:02:00,496 --> 00:02:02,272
Hey, where's the drum roll?

51
00:02:02,272 --> 00:02:03,424
It was too annoying.

52
00:02:03,424 --> 00:02:04,576
Then I'll make my own.

53
00:02:04,576 --> 00:02:06,128
Bedededelluhmm... eh-

54
00:02:06,128 --> 00:02:13,200
PBPBPBPBPBPBPBPBpbpbpbpbpbpb...

55
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:15,520
[GASP!] KSSHHHHH!

56
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:16,832
Spongy gets a cake...

57
00:02:16,832 --> 00:02:17,952
Yaaay!

58
00:02:17,952 --> 00:02:19,392
...and David is eliminated.

59
00:02:19,392 --> 00:02:21,008
Aw, seriously?!

60
00:02:23,056 --> 00:02:24,784
Whoa! That-that was just-

61
00:02:24,784 --> 00:02:28,720
Yes, it was our double
laser-powered teleportation device.

62
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:29,744
♪ [INTRO PLAYS] ♪

63
00:02:29,888 --> 00:02:32,496
Wait, we already played that, didn't we?

64
00:02:32,496 --> 00:02:36,976
Well, yeah, you did. But let's play it
again, you know, for good measure.

65
00:02:36,976 --> 00:02:43,712
♪ [INTRO PLAYS] ♪

66
00:02:46,544 --> 00:02:49,392
Wow, Firey! It's such a
relief that David's eliminated.

67
00:02:49,392 --> 00:02:50,192
Definitely.

68
00:02:50,192 --> 00:02:51,152
He was weird.

69
00:02:51,152 --> 00:02:54,400
I know! He looked a lot
like a human, whatever that is.

70
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:56,192
You know, Firey, I think we should be friends!

71
00:02:56,192 --> 00:02:57,968
You mean, like, form an alliance?

72
00:02:57,968 --> 00:03:00,352
No! Friends, j-just friends, friends.

73
00:03:00,352 --> 00:03:01,920
Yeah! We could do that.

74
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:02,688
Let's do it!

75
00:03:02,688 --> 00:03:04,032
I want to be friends, too.

76
00:03:04,032 --> 00:03:05,104
Gah! Get away!

77
00:03:05,104 --> 00:03:08,288
Why are you excluding me? I just want to be friends.

78
00:03:08,288 --> 00:03:10,624
Sorry, only good people get to be friends.

79
00:03:10,624 --> 00:03:12,160
Ooh! Burn!

80
00:03:12,272 --> 00:03:14,608
Anyway, I'm giving all of you immunity.

81
00:03:15,088 --> 00:03:18,016
However, it is possible for you to lose your immunity.

82
00:03:18,016 --> 00:03:21,328
- And how could that happen?
- Oh, you could be hit by an asteroid.

83
00:03:21,536 --> 00:03:24,208
Or abducted by aliens, to name a few.

84
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:26,144
ROCKY:
Bleh!

85
00:03:31,584 --> 00:03:32,624
Moving on...

86
00:03:32,832 --> 00:03:36,208
The twentieth contest is to
get into a spaceship. Go.

87
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,456
Hueughauuugh!

88
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:39,680
- Hup! Did it!
- Hup! Did it!

89
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,760
Ah! Oh, no! I can't get in!

90
00:03:42,208 --> 00:03:44,896
If you get hit by anything, you lose your immunity.

91
00:03:44,896 --> 00:03:45,728
Yikes!

92
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:47,904
Aaaghueughehhh!

93
00:03:48,896 --> 00:03:51,408
Hey, Fir-AYE! Let's go get Spongy!

94
00:03:51,408 --> 00:03:52,224
Yeah!

95
00:03:52,224 --> 00:03:53,280
SPONGY:
Huh?

96
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:58,080
Huh-whoa! Whoa! Whoa-ughuoahooaaaaughhugh!

97
00:03:58,080 --> 00:04:00,080
Whoa-whoa-WHOA-urghruoah!

98
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:02,848
We're not getting him, Leafy!
Time for super-speed mode!

99
00:04:02,848 --> 00:04:04,400
But don't you know how much energy that wastes?

100
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,229
- You have to be more eco-friendly, I mean-

101
00:04:05,229 --> 00:04:06,400
- SPONGY: Grr!
- You have to be more eco-friendly, I mean-

102
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,400
Oh, no! Leafy! No!

103
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,752
Huh? Why am I moving?

104
00:04:13,312 --> 00:04:14,944
Oh, my gosh! What's that?

105
00:04:14,944 --> 00:04:18,448
Falling into that black hole will also
cause you to lose your immunity.

106
00:04:18,448 --> 00:04:19,488
BUBBLE:
Oh noio!

107
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:20,720
SPONGY:
Uh-oh.

108
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:23,968
AAAAAAHHHHH!

109
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,808
HAAAAEUUUH!

110
00:04:25,808 --> 00:04:26,656
WAAAAUUGH!

111
00:04:26,656 --> 00:04:28,480
Hey! Where'd it go?

112
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:30,864
We had to sell it because of budget cuts.

113
00:04:30,864 --> 00:04:33,520
Weird. Hey, where'd my spaceship go?

114
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:34,176
Same thing.

115
00:04:34,176 --> 00:04:36,170
Oh, well, I still have MINE!

116
00:04:37,328 --> 00:04:38,624
And Bubble wins immunity.

117
00:04:38,624 --> 00:04:39,696
YOYLECAKE!

118
00:04:40,016 --> 00:04:42,224
Now, let's recover the lost contestants.

119
00:04:48,910 --> 00:04:53,616
Bubble, as another reward, you get to choose
another person to also have immunity.

120
00:04:53,616 --> 00:04:56,992
Oh, uh, okay. Uh...give it to Leafy

121
00:04:56,992 --> 00:04:59,936
to prove to her that I am a nice person after all...

122
00:04:59,936 --> 00:05:00,944
AGAIN!!!

123
00:05:01,072 --> 00:05:02,940
Twice in a row? That's quite nice.

124
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:06,848
Ooh, yay! Quite nice is a lot
better than what I got last time!

125
00:05:06,848 --> 00:05:08,640
Well, it is better, but not by much.

126
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:11,968
You still got seventy-three more levels to go
before you reach my level of niceness.

127
00:05:11,968 --> 00:05:13,552
Oh! Awh...

128
00:05:13,552 --> 00:05:15,712
That means Bubble and Leafy have immunity,

129
00:05:15,712 --> 00:05:19,952
while Ice Cube, Rocky, Spongy,
and Firey are up for elimination.

130
00:05:20,464 --> 00:05:21,744
And guess what?

131
00:05:21,744 --> 00:05:25,296
The fifteen eliminated contestants
will get to choose who to eliminate.

132
00:05:25,536 --> 00:05:27,600
And they will have one month to decide.

133
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,304
[GASP!]

134
00:05:28,304 --> 00:05:31,664
Do you hear that, voters? That means
you will vote on something else.

135
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:33,660
And what would this something else be?

136
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:37,152
You see, an eliminated contestant's
going to rejoin the game.

137
00:05:37,152 --> 00:05:38,032
[GASP!]

138
00:05:38,896 --> 00:05:41,328
For the last time in BFDI, ever.

139
00:05:41,328 --> 00:05:42,320
[GASP!]

140
00:05:42,864 --> 00:05:44,992
And the voters will decide who it is.

141
00:05:44,992 --> 00:05:46,048
[GASP!]

142
00:05:46,496 --> 00:05:49,040
Oh, be quiet, you gaspers.

143
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:52,240
So anyways, voters, I really want you to vote.

144
00:05:52,528 --> 00:05:53,648
You can choose Flower....

145
00:05:53,648 --> 00:05:56,672
You'd better vote me, or-or I'll stretch you!

146
00:05:56,672 --> 00:05:59,920
- ANNOUNCER: Blocky...
- Come on, guys! I really deserve a third chance.

147
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:01,824
- ANNOUNCER: Woody...
- Ahh... Ehhh...

148
00:06:01,824 --> 00:06:05,024
- ANNOUNCER: Pin...
- Vote for me, and I will make improvements

149
00:06:05,024 --> 00:06:07,152
to the show of Battle for Dream Island!

150
00:06:07,152 --> 00:06:08,816
- ANNOUNCER: Needy...
- Don't call me Needy!

151
00:06:08,816 --> 00:06:10,128
- ANNOUNCER:
Needy. Needy. Needy.

152
00:06:10,128 --> 00:06:11,040
- ANNOUNCER:
Teardrop...

153
00:06:11,488 --> 00:06:12,304
- ANNOUNCER:
Golf Ball...

154
00:06:12,304 --> 00:06:15,472
I have a 6.666 repeating
percent chance on joining the game,

155
00:06:15,472 --> 00:06:19,536
and if I rejoin, I'll have a 16.666 repeating
percent chance of winning Dream Island.

156
00:06:19,660 --> 00:06:23,472
So, from this moment, I have a 1.111 repeating
percent chance of winning Dream Island.

157
00:06:23,472 --> 00:06:26,000
- ANNOUNCER: Coiny...
- Viewers! All you people out there!

158
00:06:26,192 --> 00:06:30,320
I mean, yeah, I love you guys – you're all my
friends – but just-just think for a moment.

159
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:34,080
Does it really make sense that someone
as stupid as Firey is in the game,

160
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:36,304
yet someone-someone like me is not?

161
00:06:36,304 --> 00:06:39,312
Just-just think about that for a moment
and the answer will come to you:

162
00:06:39,312 --> 00:06:40,816
the person that you think should win!

163
00:06:40,816 --> 00:06:43,792
- ANNOUNCER: Snowball...
- I'm the only one who really deserves Dream Island!

164
00:06:43,792 --> 00:06:45,790
The rest are all WEAK LOSERS!

165
00:06:46,384 --> 00:06:48,016
- ANNOUNCER: Match...
- OMG!

166
00:06:48,016 --> 00:06:51,568
Vote for, like, me, and plus, I dyed my hair, like, blue.

167
00:06:51,568 --> 00:06:52,576
ANNOUNCER:
Eraser...

168
00:06:52,992 --> 00:06:56,240
Hey! This rejoin button isn't working.

169
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,840
- ANNOUNCER: Pen...
- If you vote for me,

170
00:06:57,840 --> 00:07:01,328
I will give you 500 million
vigintillion dollars!

171
00:07:01,328 --> 00:07:05,984
- ANNOUNCER: That clumsy Tennis Ball...
- You know, Announcer, I wouldn't say that if I were you.

172
00:07:05,984 --> 00:07:09,408
I've got a magnet, and I can DEMAGNETIZE you!

173
00:07:09,408 --> 00:07:10,192
ANNOUNCER:
Yikes!

174
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:12,576
- ANNOUNCER: Pencil...
- ♪ Vote for me, yeah yeah yeah! ♪

175
00:07:12,576 --> 00:07:14,208
♪ Type my name, yeah yeah yeah! ♪

176
00:07:14,208 --> 00:07:16,096
♪ So I can rejoin the contest, ♪

177
00:07:16,096 --> 00:07:18,090
♪ So I can rejoin the contest! ♪

178
00:07:18,090 --> 00:07:20,256
- ANNOUNCER: and David.
- Aw, seriously?!

179
00:07:20,256 --> 00:07:22,000
- ANNOUNCER: Say something else.
- NO!

180
00:07:22,448 --> 00:07:24,784
Cast a vote by commenting on this video.

181
00:07:29,952 --> 00:07:35,104
I was wondering: how are we in space, yet able
to talk, paddle, breathe, and not explode?

182
00:07:35,424 --> 00:07:36,704
Budget cuts.